I remember the exact moment I understood that good leadership could save a life.

I was at a community health center in an underserved Nairobi ward. A mother had walked six kilometers carrying her child — severe fever, barely conscious. The health center had no malaria test kits. They had been out of stock for three weeks.

I started calling. The sub-county health officer. A nearby hospital. A friend who worked at a pharmacy in town. Within four hours, we had the test kits. The child was diagnosed, treated, and walked home the next day with medicine and hope.

That day taught me a truth I carry into this campaign: **our problems are solvable.** What we lack is not resources. It is leadership with the will to make things work.

## Why I am running

I am running for Governor because I have seen what happens when government shows up. I have seen health centers run smoothly under competent management. I have seen young people build careers after real skills training. I have seen communities transform when clean water and good roads arrive.

And I have seen the alternative.

Too many health centers are understaffed. Too many young graduates have no path to employment. Too many families still carry water on their heads. These are solvable problems — and they persist only because leadership has failed to solve them.

## My commitment to you

I do not ask for your vote. I ask for your trust — and I will earn it by delivering measurable progress in the first 100 days of my administration.

This campaign is not about me. It is about the people of Nairobi County coming together to demand the leadership we deserve.

Join us. The change starts now.

— Bill Llia
